1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,200
The Romans lived in Britain between 43AD and 410AD but their legacy is still felt today and not just in physical ruins.
罗马人于公元43年至公元410年期间居住在不列颠，但他们留下的遗产至今仍能被感知到，这不仅仅体现在那些实体遗迹上。

2
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:22,470
The Romans left us language, including some common English words.
罗马人还给我们留下了语言财富，其中包括一些常用的英语单词。

3
00:00:22,470 --> 00:00:31,420
During the Roman Empire, Latin, an ancient language, was spoken in many parts of Britain.
在罗马帝国时期，拉丁语这门古老的语言在不列颠的许多地区被使用。

4
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:45,210
While the Romans wrote in classical Latin, they conversed in vulgar Latin – colloquial, everyday language that was used between soldiers and in trade.
罗马人书写时用的是古典拉丁语，但日常交谈时则使用通俗拉丁语——这种口语的日常用语在士兵之间以及贸易往来中被广泛使用。

5
00:00:45,210 --> 00:00:56,040
Because of trade, words that stuck often relate to food and drink, such as ‘wine’, which came from the Latin ‘vinum’.
由于贸易的缘故，留存下来的词汇往往与饮食相关，比如“wine（葡萄酒）”一词，就源自拉丁语中的“vinum”。

6
00:00:56,040 --> 00:01:09,090
Others relate to dwellings such as ‘kitchen’, derived from the verb ‘cook’, and ‘wall’, which originally referred to a stake or post outside a fort.
还有一些词汇与住所相关，例如“kitchen（厨房）”衍生自拉丁语中的动词“cook（烹饪）”，而“wall（墙）”最初指的是堡垒外的木桩或柱子。

7
00:01:09,090 --> 00:01:14,480
Settlements and roads in Roman times were extensive.
罗马时期的定居点和道路广泛分布于各地。

8
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:27,170
The word ‘street’, used generally as well as being used for specific names of streets, originally came from ‘strata’ which meant paved road.
“street（街道）”一词如今既可以泛指街道，也用于具体的街道名称中，它最初源自拉丁语中的“strata”，意为“铺砌的道路”。

9
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:40,160
On a similar note, academic research from the field of linguistics indicates many well-known place names in the UK owe their origin to Latin.
同样，语言学领域的学术研究表明，英国许多著名的地名都起源于拉丁语。

10
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:53,190
For example, the Romans used ‘castrum’ to refer to a city, which developed into the common place ending -chester, -caster or -cester.
例如，罗马人用“castrum”指代城市，这个词后来演变成了常见的地名后缀“-chester”“-caster”或“-cester”。

11
00:01:53,190 --> 00:02:01,600
Consider Manchester. It is a former Roman fort which was known as Mamuciam.
以曼彻斯特（Manchester）为例，它曾是一座罗马堡垒，当时名为“Mamuciam”。

12
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:07,730
Other places with Roman derivations include Lancaster and Leicester.
其他罗马派生出来的地名还包括兰卡斯特（Lancaster）和莱斯特（Leicester）。

13
00:02:07,730 --> 00:02:15,600
A significant impact on English which came from the Romans is the use of the Roman alphabet.
罗马人对英语产生的一个重要影响是罗马字母表的使用。

14
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:23,250
Manuscripts of Old English texts have shown a version not unalike written English today.
古英语文本的手稿显示，当时的书写形式与如今的书面英语已有相似之处。

15
00:02:23,250 --> 00:02:30,890
Differences include some letters however, such as two symbols called ‘ash’ and ‘eth’.
不过两者之间也存在一些差异，比如包含两个名为“ash（æ）”和“eth（ð）”的符号。

16
00:02:30,890 --> 00:02:37,210
Nowadays you are more likely to see these symbols in a guide to pronunciation.
如今，你更有可能在发音指南中看到这些符号。

17
00:02:37,210 --> 00:02:44,660
So, even though 1,600 years have passed, the Romans live on.
所以，即便1600多年已经过去，罗马人的印记依然延续至今。
